**Definition 2.1 (source coefficients and normalized moments).** Use
positive source amplitudes, written with subscripts to distinguish
various auxiliary coordinates:

$$
\begin{gathered}
D=\operatorname{diag}(h_0,h_1,h_2),\quad
T=a_K|0\rangle\langle1|+b_K|1\rangle\langle0|,\quad
S=c_K|0\rangle\langle2|+d_K|2\rangle\langle0|,\\
M=\operatorname{diag}(0,m_1,m_2),\qquad
D^\dagger D+T^\dagger T+S^\dagger S+M=I_3,\\
\kappa=h_0a_K+h_1b_K>0,\quad\kappa_{02}=h_0c_K+h_2d_K>0,\\
\theta=\frac{a_Kb_K}{h_0h_1},\quad
\omega=\frac{c_Kd_K}{h_0h_2},\quad
\delta=\theta+\omega<1,\quad s_0=\sqrt\delta,\\
A_y=\sum_i h_i^2p_{yi},\quad
B_y=b_K^2p_{y0}+a_K^2p_{y1},\quad
C_y=d_K^2p_{y0}+c_K^2p_{y2}.
\end{gathered}
\tag{EP.10}
$$

The scalar $B_y$ is not the ideal live matrix. These three resource
functions are positive and strictly increasing through $5,16,27$.
JR34–40 supplies $\mathsf C(s)=(1-\delta)A_{27}$ for
$0\leq s\leq s_0$. Set $\Delta=\rho_{27,+,+}-\rho_{5,+,+}$,
$(K_0,K_1,K_2)=(D,T,S)$ only in the following definition of $N$, and

$$
\begin{gathered}
N_{ij}=\operatorname{tr}(K_i\Delta K_j^\dagger),\quad
L=\operatorname{diag}(s_0,1,1),\quad L_0=L^2,\quad G=LNL
 =\begin{pmatrix}g_0&x&y\\x&g_1&z\\y&z&g_2\end{pmatrix},\\
\beta=\omega/\delta,\quad\alpha=1-\beta,\quad\gamma=\alpha/\beta,\quad
Q=\operatorname{diag}(1,-\alpha,-\beta),\quad
Q_0=\operatorname{diag}(1,-\theta,-\omega),\quad LQ_0L=\delta Q,\\
C=(e_0e_1^T+e_1e_0^T)/2,\quad\tau=s/s_0,\quad j(\tau)=J_{s_0\tau}.
\end{gathered}
\tag{EP.11}
$$

In particular $\operatorname{tr}(CX)=X_{01}$. The $x,y,z$ entries of
$G$ are not the original height, height index or CG coordinate. Write
$\Delta A=A_{27}-A_5$, and similarly for $B,C$. With
$\xi=\kappa(q_{27}-q_5)$,
$\eta=\kappa_{02}(\sqrt{27}-\sqrt5)/16$ and
$\zeta=a_Kc_K(\sqrt{37}-\sqrt{59})/16$,

$$
N=\begin{pmatrix}\Delta A&\xi&\eta\\\xi&\Delta B&\zeta\\
\eta&\zeta&\Delta C\end{pmatrix},\qquad
(g_0,g_1,g_2,x,y,z)=(\delta\Delta A,\Delta B,\Delta C,s_0\xi,s_0\eta,\zeta).
\tag{EP.12}
$$

Define the unnormalized failure difference, extended by zero on
coordinate $0$, by

$$
\begin{gathered}
\Xi=M^{1/2}\Delta M^{1/2}\big|_{\{1,2\}}
 =\begin{pmatrix}-d_f&z_f\\z_f&0\end{pmatrix},\quad
d_f=11m_1/64,\quad
z_f=\sqrt{m_1m_2}(\sqrt{37}-\sqrt{59})/16\ne0,\\
L_f=\sqrt{d_f^2+4z_f^2},\quad
T_{\rm flat}=\frac{(1-\delta)\Delta A+L_f+\operatorname{tr}G}{2}
            =\frac{d_f+L_f}{2}.
\end{gathered}
\tag{EP.13}
$$

The trace identity in EP.10 gives
$\Delta A+\Delta B+\Delta C=d_f$. All expressions are evaluated at
the conditional source point. Box enclosures used for signs do not
make off-root points normalized channels.

